 data-label="register" class="panel_button register_button" data-register_action="header" href="/register">Register</a></div></div><div class="header_dropdown" data-target="browse"><a href="/games/store">Indie game store</a><a href="/games/free">Free games</a><a href="/games/fun">Fun games</a><a href="/games/tag-horror">Horror games</a><div class="divider"></div><a href="/tools">Game development</a><a href="/game-assets">Assets</a><a href="/comics">Comics</a><div class="divider"></div><a href="/sales">Sales</a><a href="/bundles">Bundles</a><div class="divider"></div><a href="/jobs">Jobs</a><div class="divider"></div><a href="/tags">Tags</a><a href="/game-development/engines">Game Engines</a></div></div><div class="jam_page_wrap" id="wrapper"><div class="view_jam_page view_jam_base_page page_widget base_widget view_jam_default during_voting" id="view_jam_1843955"><div class="jam_banner_outer"><img class="jam_banner full_width"/></div><div class="jam_body"><div class="jam_header_widget base_widget" id="jam_header_3520931"><div class="header_inner"><div class="header_columns"><div class="title_colum"><h1 class="jam_title_header"><a href="/jam/pirate">Pirate Software - Game Jam 19</a></h1><div class="jam_host_header">Hosted by <a href="https://piratesoftware.itch.io">Pirate Software</a> · <a href="https://bsky.app/hashtag/PirateJam">#PirateJam</a></div></div><div class="stats_container"><div class="stat_box"><a href="/jam/pirate/entries"><div class="stat_value">53</div><div class="stat_label">Entries</div></a></div><div class="stat_box"><div class="stat_value">285</div><div class="stat_label">Ratings</div></div></div></div><div class="header_tabs"><a data-label="tab_view_jam" class="header_tab active" href="/jam/pirate">Overview</a><a data-label="tab_view_jam_entries" class="header_tab" href="/jam/pirate/entries">Submissions</a><a data-label="tab_view_jam_feed" class="header_tab" href="/jam/pirate/feed">Submission feed</a></div></div></div><div class="submitter_outer"><div class="jam_submitter_widget base_widget during_voting" id="jam_submitter_6484430"><div class="date_data">Submissions open from <span data-format="MMMM Do YYYY [at] h:mm A" class="date_format">2026-07-15 13:00:00</span> to <span data-format="MMMM Do YYYY [at] h:mm A" class="date_format">2026-07-31 13:00:00</span></div><div class="countdown"><span class="countdown_label">Voting ends in</span><div class="times"><div data-name="years" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">years</div></div><div data-name="months" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">months</div></div><div data-name="days" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">days</div></div><div data-name="hours" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">hours</div></div><div data-name="minutes" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">minutes</div></div><div data-name="seconds" class="time_block"><div class="block_value"></div><div class="block_label">seconds</div></div></div></div><div class="state_action">Submission is closed and voting is now in progress</div></div></div><div class="jam_content user_formatted"><h1 class="text-center"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgxNzMyLnBuZw==/original/jnpgve.png" loading="lazy"></h1>
<h1 class="text-center">What is a GameJam?</h1>
<p>A Game Jam is a short event where you and others work together to create a small game. Most Jams have some kind of restriction on theme or style to get you thinking about games in a new way. Game Jams are a great way to test ideas, build on your skills, and meet other awesome creative people. Do them. Future you will thank you for it. Pirate Software runs Game Jams two times a year and all of our jams have prizes!</p>
<h1 class="text-center"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgxNzI4LnBuZw==/original/e0x8%2BG.png" loading="lazy"></h1>
<h1 class="text-center">Can I make a game?</h1>
<h3 class="text-center">Yes you can.</h3>
<div class="text-center"><iframe width="700" height="394" src="//www.youtube.com/embed/aMc-GKv5olA" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div>
<h1 class="text-center"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgxNzI4LnBuZw==/original/e0x8%2BG.png" loading="lazy"></h1>
<h1 class="text-center">Theme</h1>
<h3 class="text-center">The Cost of Progress</h3>
<ul>Everything has a price. As people progress through your game they will need to pay something to keep going. Maybe they run a cult and their patron requires sacrifices. Maybe they&#x27;ve been Isekai&#x27;d into a Triple A game and only microtransactions will save them. Maybe they&#x27;re an introvert at a party and need to pay social battery to make friends. Maybe it&#x27;s something as simple as running a toll booth. The choice is yours so keep an open mind on this and don&#x27;t let it stop you. After all, the difficulty here is your cost to progress.<p></p>
</ul>
<h1 class="text-center"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgxNzMyLnBuZw==/original/jnpgve.png" loading="lazy"></h1>
<h1 class="text-center">Setup</h1>
<ul>
<li>Join our official <a href="https://discord.gg/piratesoftware" rel="nofollow noopener" referrerpolicy="origin">Discord</a>!</li>
<li>Form up into teams or decide on running solo.</li>
<li>Come up with a team name and get ready to jam!</li>
</ul>
<h1 class="text-center"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgxNzI1LnBuZw==/original/rRhPOq.png" loading="lazy"></h1>
<h1 class="text-center">Rules</h1>
<ul>
<li>This is not an exhaustive list. Don&#x27;t be a dumbass. 👺</li>
<li>You must follow the <a href="https://itch.io/docs/legal/terms">Itch.io TOS.</a></li>
<li>No teams of more than 5 people.</li>
<li>Your submission must include a <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Vl7BMvzUOhbunJrI_X1gUc6x-LAp3aaBiPwHUf27B70/edit#heading=h.lr899156xjnx" rel="nofollow noopener" referrerpolicy="origin">Game Design Document</a>.</li>
<li>If you do need to leave let your team know in advance.</li>
<li>Do not attempt to sabotage other teams.</li>
<li>No AI-Generated Content of any kind.</li>
<li>No Pornographic Content or Nudity.</li>
<li>No Illicit Drug References.</li>
<li>You can only use assets you have the commercial license for.
<br>Some asset packs only allow non-commercial use.
<br>Make sure you know the licensing limits for anything you use.
<br>The intention is for you to build your own stuff and learn from it.
<br>Don&#x27;t overthink this and try to find a way around it, just make things.
<br>The game jam is a flex of personal skill not personal wallet. -Zafaroth</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<p><br></p>
<h1 class="text-center"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgxNzI4LnBuZw==/original/e0x8%2BG.png" loading="lazy"></h1>
<h1 class="text-center">Submission</h1>
<h3>Game Design Document</h3>
<ul>
<li>This is a planning document that details what your game will be.</li>
<li>This is a required part of your submission and a best practice so don&#x27;t forget it!</li>
<li>You MUST submit your GDD as a Google Drive file not a downloadable PDF</li>
<li><a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Vl7BMvzUOhbunJrI_X1gUc6x-LAp3aaBiPwHUf27B70" rel="nofollow noopener" referrerpolicy="origin">You can read a sample GDD here!</a></li></ul>
<h3>Prototype</h3>
<ul>
<li>This is a very limited working copy of your game.</li>
<li>Focus on playability over anything else.</li>
<li>If it doesn&#x27;t run, it won&#x27;t win.</li>
<li>Your Prototype MUST run as a browser upload here on itch.io.</li>
<li>The reason this is required is for ease of judging and reduction in malware.</li>
<li>Winners will be announced during the daily <a href="https://piratesoftware.live/" style="" rel="nofollow noopener" referrerpolicy="origin">Dev Stream!</a></li>
</ul>
<h1 class="text-center"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgxNzI4LnBuZw==/original/e0x8%2BG.png" loading="lazy"></h1>
<h1 class="text-center">Voting Criteria</h1>
<p>If you submitted a game you can vote on any of the other games in the Jam. You&#x27;ll be able to vote on five major categories for each game. As games are subjective media these categories are guidelines for you to follow when exploring. Don&#x27;t worry about tricking others into liking your game. Just focus on making the best game you can. Don&#x27;t overthink it.</p>
<h3>Playability</h3>
<ul>
<li>Were systems in the game clunky or polished?</li>
<li>Did the game run without crashes and hangs?</li>
<li>This is the most important category and counts for a lot.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Theme Implementation</h3>
<ul>
<li>Did the game follow the theme?</li>
<li>Was the theme entirely ignored?</li>
<li>Did they implement the theme in a clever and interesting way?</li>
</ul>
<h3>Game Design Document</h3>
<ul>
<li>Did they create a well written Design Doc?</li>
<li>Did the game end up drifting from their vision?</li>
<li>Did they keep the document up to date as their ideas changed?</li>
</ul>
<h3>Artistic Style</h3>
<ul>
<li>Everyone has a style that they like or enjoy.</li>
<li>Style is not bound only to Triple A assets from major studios.</li>
<li>Pixel Art, Midi Songs, Foley work and more all ooze with artistic style.</li>
<li>Just make something YOU think works and run with it.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Community Choice</h3>
<ul>
<li>Sometimes you just like a game and don&#x27;t need a specific reason why.</li>
<li>This category is for each of your favorite games to add extra weight to them.</li>
</ul>
<h1 class="text-center"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgxNzI4LnBuZw==/original/e0x8%2BG.png" loading="lazy"></h1>
<h1 class="text-center">Prizes</h1>
<h5 class="text-center">
<img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzI0OTY1NTc1LnBuZw==/original/LxRNd7.png" style="width: 80%" loading="lazy">
</h5>
<h1 class="text-center"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgxNzMyLnBuZw==/original/jnpgve.png" loading="lazy"></h1>
<h1 class="text-center">Socials</h1>
<h5 class="text-center">
<a href="https://discord.gg/piratesoftware" rel="nofollow noopener" referrerpolicy="origin"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgyMzM2LnBuZw==/original/g5I1N0.png" style="width: 75px" loading="lazy"></a>      
<a href="https://twitch.tv/piratesoftware" rel="nofollow noopener" referrerpolicy="origin"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTkzNDAxLnBuZw==/original/%2BwAEVE.png" style="width: 75px" loading="lazy"></a>      
<a href="https://youtube.com/c/piratesoftware" rel="nofollow noopener" referrerpolicy="origin"><img src="https://img.itch.zone/aW1nLzE0MTgyMzQxLnBuZw==/original/mHnsid.png" style="width: 75px" loading="lazy"></a>
